1
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,340
Monica? Hey, can I borrow the Porsche?

2
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:12,260
Okay.

3
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:12,260
All right!

4
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:14,840
But, uh, ahem, what is it not?

5
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:18,430
A place to entertain my lady friends.

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:23,520
And what else is it not?

7
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:23,520
A place to eat spaghetti.

8
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,230
Very good.

9
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,230
Thanks.

10
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,590
What do you need it for anyway?

11
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:28,940
The, uh, lottery is up to 300 million...

12
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:31,350
and they don't sell tickets here.

13
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:33,650
So you're driving up to Connecticut?

14
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,030
Yeah, Connecticut. Not West Virginia.

15
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:41,870
Maybe I'll drive you up there. I'd like to buy some tickets myself.

16
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:46,460
Yeah, with Chandler not getting paid, we could really use $300 million.

17
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:49,010
Yes, because if I was at my old job,

18
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:51,550
we'd say, "300 million? No, thank you."

19
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,470
Will you get me tickets too?

20
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,470
Yeah, me too.

21
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:57,340
Sure.

22
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:57,340
Ooh! I have an idea.

23
00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:00,770
Why don't we all pitch in 50 bucks, we'll pool our money together...

24
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:04,640
and then if we win, we'll split it.

25
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:04,640
That's a great idea!

26
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,520
No, thanks.

27
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:10,520
You don't want to win the lottery?

28
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:10,520
Uh, sure I do.

29
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:12,690
I also want to be king of my own country...

30
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:15,650
and find out what happened to Amelia Earhart.

31
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:19,410
Still on Amelia Earhart?

32
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:19,410
The woman just vanished!

33
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,910
Seriously, you don't want in on this?

34
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:26,040
No. Do you know what your odds are of winning the lottery?

35
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:29,840
I mean, you have a better chance of being struck by lightning 42 times.

36
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:33,210
But there's six of us, so we'd only have to get struck 7 times.

37
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,590
I like those odds!

38
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:40,300
Seriously, you guys, I can't believe you're gonna spend $250 on the lottery.

39
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:43,720
I mean, that's such a bunch of boo-hockey.

40
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:48,980
I'll ask.

41
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:51,230
"Boo-hockey"?

42
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:54,360
Oh, we think Emma's about to start talking...

43
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:58,160
so we're trying to be careful about what words we use in front of her.

44
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,530
So get ready to hear a lot of, uh, boo-hockey...

45
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,290
gosh darn it and brother pucker.

46
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:06,910
How do you know she's gonna start talking?

47
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:10,380
When I talk to her, I almost feel like she understands what I'm saying.

48
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,950
Kind of like Joey.

49
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:16,220
What's that now?

50
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:13,060
God, look at all these tickets. It's so exciting.

51
00:03:13,270 --> 00:03:15,230
I haven't won anything since sixth grade.

52
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,740
Pie-eating contest?

53
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:23,070
You assume because I was heavy that's the only way I could win something?

54
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,290
No, I saw a picture of you covered in blueberries.

55
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:29,330
That was a good day.

56
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:29,330
Yeah.

57
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:33,880
They're towing your car!

58
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:33,880
I'm parked in a garage on Morton.

59
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:37,300
They're towing a car.

60
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:41,180
And I am seeing spots.

61
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:44,050
Ross, you don't have Emma! Rachel, you don't have Emma!

62
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,640
Where's Emma? Who has Emma?

63
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,640
Joey, relax.

64
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:51,100
My mother picked her up two hours ago. You were there.

65
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,900
I was?

66
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,900
Yes, and you talked to her.

67
00:03:55,310 --> 00:03:58,400
I did?

68
00:03:55,310 --> 00:03:58,400
She dropped off a casserole.

69
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:01,570
Oh, yeah, the casserole lady.

70
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:04,160
Did you come by to watch us win the big bucks?

71
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:07,950
Yeah. And then I figured after you win, we can all go out to the balcony...

72
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:11,620
and see a night rainbow with gremlins dancing on top of it.

73
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:16,000
Don't touch the phone! I'll get it! I'll get it!

74
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,120
You think he washed his hands?

75
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,120
Hello?

76
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,630
Hey, Charlie, what do you know?

77
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,630
What's going on?

78
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:24,710
Chandler's supposed to find out if he's getting a job at his agency.

79
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,640
But out of 15 interns, they're only hiring three.

80
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,640
Ooh. Tough odds.

81
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,640
Yeah.

82
00:04:29,850 --> 00:04:33,600
If only it were a sure thing like your 24-state lottery.

83
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:38,440
Yeah, look who's coming around!

84
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:42,360
Damn it. All right, call me when you know more.

85
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,570
Did you get it?

86
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,570
One of the slots got filled.

87
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:51,500
By you?

88
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:51,500
Sense the tone.

89
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:56,330
No, that kid Nate got it.

90
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:56,330
Oh, I hate that guy.

91
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,750
I mean, come on, pull up your pants!

92
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,750
I know.

93
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,800
Well, there's two spots left, right?

94
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,630
Yeah. I mean, I want this so much. I want to get one.

95
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,010
I want my friend Charlie to get one.

96
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,260
Except I don't care about Charlie.

97
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:12,220
Hey!

98
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:15,140
You are not gonna believe this. I just saw my psychic...

99
00:05:15,310 --> 00:05:19,190
and she said I was definitely gonna win the lottery tonight!

100
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,650
I thought we could use some extra luck...

101
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:24,860
so I brought a wishbone home from work.

102
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:31,540
A psychic and a wishbone? Guys, give someone else a chance.

103
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,080
All right, who wants to do it?

104
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,080
Ooh, can I?

105
00:05:34,290 --> 00:05:37,250
Vegetarians never get to do the wishbone.

106
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:40,250
It's really not fair. Just because we don't eat the meat...

107
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:43,510
doesn't mean we don't like to play with the carcasses.

108
00:05:44,130 --> 00:05:45,840
All right. Rash'?

109
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:48,430
I don't want that turkey smell all over my hands.

110
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:52,180
I'll do it! It'll get the casserole stink off of mine.

111
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,270
I hope I win.

112
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,270
Well, it doesn't really matter.

113
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,400
You're both wishing for the same thing.

114
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:04,360
I can't tell you what I'm wishing for, or else, you know, it won't come true. Ha, ha.

115
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:07,610
Right. But we know what you're wishing for.

116
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:10,780
I can't really say.

117
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:10,780
I understand.

118
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:13,490
But you're wishing for what we think, aren't you?

119
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:16,460
I'm not really comfortable with these questions!

120
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:18,710
Please!

121
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:18,710
Just do it!

122
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,880
Okay. One, two, three.

123
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,960
I won! Hey!

124
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:26,260
You know what? I'm sure your wish is gonna come true.

125
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:29,970
But, you guys, just in case, maybe a genie will come out if we rub this lamp.

126
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,680
Ow!

127
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,640
That thing gets hot!

128
00:06:34,810 --> 00:06:36,480
Ross, just keep making yourjokes.

129
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,850
How are you gonna feel if we actually do win?

130
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:42,230
Uh, you're not gonna win.

131
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:42,230
I know the odds are against us...

132
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:46,570
but somebody has to win, and it could be us. And then how you gonna feel?

133
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:50,490
We're gonna be like, "Everybody, let's take our helicopters up to the Cape."

134
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:53,030
And you're gonna be all, like, "Oh, I can't, guys.

135
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:56,410
I'll have to meet you up there. I gotta gas up the Hyundai."

136
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:04,590
Okay, I've heard myself on tape, and I sound nothing like that.

137
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:07,970
I can see the headline now: "Lottery Winners' Friend...

138
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:10,550
Filled With Regret, Eats Own Arm."

139
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,720
Why would I eat my own arm?

140
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:16,520
Well, you wouldn't, but we own the paper. We can print whatever we want.

141
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:19,310
You know what? I'm gonna throw in 50 bucks for you.

142
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,900
Why?

143
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,900
Because I know that you think...

144
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:25,150
that the lottery is boo-hockey...

145
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:29,070
but we're all here, and we're gonna watch the numbers and have fun.

146
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:33,240
And you're my brother, and I want you to be a part of this.

147
00:07:33,950 --> 00:07:37,660
You don't have to do that. I mean, I'll pay for myself.

148
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:41,710
But just the fact that you want me to have fun with you guys, that's so sweet.

149
00:07:41,870 --> 00:07:43,500
Come here.

150
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:47,000
Get a room.

151
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:53,010
So now that you're in, what are you gonna do if we win?

152
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:57,850
I don't know. I'll probably just invest it.

153
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:57,850
Ooh. Calm down.

154
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,810
Seriously, that's your fantasy? To invest it?

155
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:03,290
Oh, I'm sorry. Did I say,

156
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:05,730
"invest it"? I meant, "Be cool and piss it all away."

157
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:11,680
Oh! Oh! I know! We should pool all our money and buy the Knicks!

158
00:08:11,990 --> 00:08:13,860
I don't really care about the Knicks.

159
00:08:14,070 --> 00:08:16,990
You will when I pick you as starting forward.

160
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:21,410
You would do that? I never get picked!

161
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:23,790
I'm not sure a sports team is the way to go.

162
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:27,460
You won't let me buy the Knicks? I can't believe you're taking this away.

163
00:08:27,630 --> 00:08:30,800
You're right, it has been your dream for over 15 seconds.

164
00:08:32,510 --> 00:08:35,970
Uh, how long until they announce the numbers, Mommy?

165
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:40,720
I'll take this one too. Uh, "Mommy"?

166
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:43,940
Oh, I've gotten into the habit of calling Rachel "Mommy"...

167
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,980
when we're around Emma.

168
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:50,030
Which I now realize we are not.

169
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:53,070
I'm hoping that if she hears it enough...

170
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,570
it'll be her first word.

171
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,570
Oh.

172
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:57,820
Although if we're gonna do that, we should probably call me "Daddy" too.

173
00:08:59,490 --> 00:09:01,980
Mm. I like that, Daddy.

174
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:08,540
I, uh... I was just talking about Rachel.

175
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:10,840
Ooh, is Daddy getting angry?

176
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:16,180
Is Daddy gonna spank me?

177
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,350
Well, that depends.

178
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:23,270
Have you been a bad...? No, I can't.

179
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:30,940
Hello? Hello? Hey, Charlie. Did anybody else hear?

180
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:34,490
What? Susan got it? How?

181
00:09:34,650 --> 00:09:37,780
Oh, man, I would've slept with him!

182
00:09:38,530 --> 00:09:40,580
All right, bye.

183
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,790
Dude, I'm sorry. But hey, there's one spot left, right?

184
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:46,670
Well, Charlie's gonna get that.

185
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:46,670
Hey, don't say that.

186
00:09:46,830 --> 00:09:49,500
You've got just as good a chance of getting that job.

187
00:09:49,710 --> 00:09:51,380
He is the boss' son.

188
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:54,460
Come on, lottery!

189
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:54,460
Yeah!

190
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:57,340
It starts in, like, 20 minutes.

191
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:57,340
Okay, here we go.

192
00:09:57,510 --> 00:10:00,890
We need to sort through the tickets quickly to see if we've won.

193
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:03,770
So does anybody have any ideas how to organize this?

194
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:06,100
Okay, how about this:

195
00:10:06,890 --> 00:10:08,940
We divide them into six groups of 40.

196
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:12,150
The remaining 10 can be read by whoever finishes first.

197
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:15,110
I have another idea.

198
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:15,110
I'm sorry, idea time is over.

199
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,660
Well, are all the tickets in the bowl?

200
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,660
Yeah.

201
00:10:19,870 --> 00:10:23,330
What about the ones on the nightstand?

202
00:10:19,870 --> 00:10:23,330
There are no tickets there.

203
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:25,830
Yes, there are. I just saw them a few minutes ago.

204
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,910
Heh. Uh, no, you didn't. You must be mistaken.

205
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:33,840
There are 20 tickets on the nightstand.

206
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:33,840
Chandler, sense the tone.

207
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:39,720
Well, well, well. Look what Mommy found.

208
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:44,100
Okay, fine. I bought 20 extra tickets for me and Chandler.

209
00:10:45,470 --> 00:10:47,980
The psychic also said that I would be betrayed.

210
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:52,560
I can't believe this. I thought we were all in this together.

211
00:10:52,770 --> 00:10:56,110
Hey, you just got in five minutes ago!

212
00:10:52,770 --> 00:10:56,110
Three minutes ago!

213
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,820
I don't know why that's important.

214
00:10:59,030 --> 00:11:03,160
I was with you the whole time. When did you even get those?

215
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:07,870
When you were reading the dirty magazines without taking off the plastic.

216
00:11:08,210 --> 00:11:09,960
I'll show you how.

217
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:14,210
Okay. Well, Monica, suppose one of your special tickets wins?

218
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:17,210
How are you gonna feel when you win and lose your friends?

219
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:21,220
Please. If I win the lottery, you guys are not gonna leave me.

220
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:25,560
Someone gave me muffins last week. I couldn't get rid of you for three days!

221
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:29,850
Chandler, would you just tell her what she did was wrong?

222
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:32,940
She's right. You shouldn't have bought tickets just for us.

223
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,770
Let me finish.

224
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:37,570
However, it doesn't look like I'm gonna get this job...

225
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:42,070
so I can't afford to have principles. So screw you! The tickets are ours!

226
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:45,620
There's the man I married.

227
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:48,160
All right. Believe me, if you win the lottery...

228
00:11:48,330 --> 00:11:50,330
it's the last you're gonna hear from us.

229
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:55,250
Fine. Don't be my friends. I'll buy new friends.

230
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,290
Yeah, and then I'll pay for their plastic surgery

231
00:11:58,290 --> 00:12:00,420
so they look just like you!

232
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:03,220
You know what? I want my share of the tickets.

233
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:05,890
I want my tickets too! And I'm buying the Knicks!

234
00:12:06,050 --> 00:12:08,520
And Steffi Graf! Ha, ha.

235
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:11,060
Cool. Then I want mine too! And if I win...

236
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:14,400
I'm gonna put it all into a very low-yield bond!

237
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:18,940
No. You guys, we gotta keep all the tickets together.

238
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:21,150
No. No, we should divide them up...

239
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,740
and I should get extra because we used my car!

240
00:12:23,950 --> 00:12:26,660
Hey! Hey! If anybody gets extra tickets, it should be me!

241
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:31,460
This whole thing was my idea!

242
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:31,460
Yeah. Thanks for inventing the lottery!

243
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:35,040
Just give them to me, and I'll split them up!

244
00:12:35,210 --> 00:12:37,210
OW!

245
00:12:35,210 --> 00:12:37,210
Ah!

246
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:39,420
Hey

247
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:39,420
Aah!

248
00:12:40,090 --> 00:12:43,130
God, I can't take it anymore! I'm putting an end to this!

249
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:46,680
Okay, if she jumps, I get her tickets!

250
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:46,680
Wait, no, no! Hey!

251
00:12:48,470 --> 00:12:51,480
If we're not doing this together, we're not doing it at all.

252
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,980
Say goodbye to your tickets.

253
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,980
No! No! No!

254
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,770
Do not come any closer!

255
00:12:56,940 --> 00:13:00,650
Can I come a little bit closer? Valuable things are getting squished.

256
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:03,530
Now, what's more important, your friends or money?

257
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:06,110
Friends!

258
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:06,110
Money!

259
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:10,990
Friends.

260
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:14,290
Hey, Monica, what about your extra tickets?

261
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:16,500
They're all in there.

262
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:20,590
Even these five that I hid in my bra.

263
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:20,590
Monica!

264
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:23,590
Okay. Good. You guys were so scared.

265
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:26,590
There is no way I was gonna dump this...

266
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:29,390
Aah!

267
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:34,730
I think I broke your bowl.

268
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:37,690
Go! Go! Go!

269
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:56,370
What a beautiful night to be running around the street, looking for tickets.

270
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,330
And the wind sure made it fun.

271
00:14:00,170 --> 00:14:02,630
Phoebe, we lost half of them.

272
00:14:00,170 --> 00:14:02,630
So what?

273
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,920
Monica, we have the winning ticket.

274
00:14:05,090 --> 00:14:08,550
My psychic said I was gonna win, remember?

275
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:12,470
Weird your psychic didn't mention anything about the scary pigeon.

276
00:14:13,970 --> 00:14:17,600
As a matter of fact, she said that's how I'm going to die.

277
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:22,070
So excuse me for being a little skittish.

278
00:14:22,230 --> 00:14:24,400
There's two messages. This could be from work.

279
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:27,950
Oh, play them.

280
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:27,950
Okay. Here we go.

281
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:35,160
Hello. This is the pigeon from the balcony calling to apologize.

282
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:41,080
I shouldn't have knocked the tickets out of the pretty lady's hand.

283
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:46,300
It was all my fault. Not hers. Bye. Coo.

284
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:55,350
Well, I bet that was very hard for him to do.

285
00:14:57,390 --> 00:14:59,060
Hey, Chandler, it's Charlie.

286
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:01,100
This is it. Shh, Shh!

287
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:05,440
Listen, um, it turns out I got the last spot.

288
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:08,450
I'm really sorry, man. It was a lot of fun working with you

289
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:11,070
Give me a call if you want.

290
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,990
Gosh, I'm so sorry, honey.

291
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:15,700
Sorry, Chandler.

292
00:15:15,870 --> 00:15:20,790
It is so unfair. It's like that time they promoted Saundra over me at work.

293
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,710
Was she related to Ralph Lauren?

294
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:26,590
No, she was just much better at her job than me.

295
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,630
You guys, the drawing's about to start.

296
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,920
We should call my mom's and say good night to Emma...

297
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:34,010
before she goes down.

298
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:34,010
Good idea.

299
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:37,310
Honey, you're being really strong about this.

300
00:15:37,470 --> 00:15:40,020
I know how badly you wanted that job.

301
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:43,020
Yeah, you know, I really thought I deserved it.

302
00:15:43,310 --> 00:15:48,610
But let's go win the lottery. I mean, we still have a 130 chances to win, right?

303
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,660
Hundred and thirty-one.

304
00:15:53,570 --> 00:15:56,280
Yeah, good night, sweetheart. I love you.

305
00:15:56,450 --> 00:16:00,290
And remember, you're Daddy's little girl. Heh.

306
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:03,120
Phoebe's totally ruined that for me.

307
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,250
Hi, Mom. Put her back on.

308
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:10,420
Rach, they're announcing the numbers!

309
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:14,640
My God, I can already feel myself changing.

310
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:18,930
Here are your official Powerball numbers. We have 53.

311
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,640
I've got that.

312
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,640
We have one too!

313
00:16:21,810 --> 00:16:24,600
We are on the road, people!

314
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:26,980
Come on!

315
00:16:27,190 --> 00:16:32,650
Mom, please, I know you love your new lips, but I can barely understand you.

316
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:35,950
Would you please just let me say good night to my daughter?

317
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,540
And here we go. The Powerball is seven.

318
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:42,460
All right, check your numbers! Make me rich.

319
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,920
You guys, you're not gonna believe this.

320
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:49,460
I was just saying good night to Emma, and she said her first words.

321
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,760
What?

322
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,760
Well, what did she say?

323
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:54,800
She said, "Gleba"!

324
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,890
Make me rich!

325
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:04,890
Isn't that amazing?

326
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:04,890
Oh, yeah. No, no, no, that's great.

327
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:06,770
Why aren't you more excited?

328
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:11,230
Rach, heh, "gleba" is not a word.

329
00:17:11,650 --> 00:17:15,660
Well, of course it is.

330
00:17:11,650 --> 00:17:15,660
Okay. What does it mean?

331
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:18,910
Well, I don't know all the words.

332
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:22,790
You know, I'm just glad I didn't miss my daughter's first word.

333
00:17:22,950 --> 00:17:27,290
Yes you did! Gleba is a word!

334
00:17:22,950 --> 00:17:27,290
Okay. Use it in a sentence.

335
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:31,300
Okay. Uh, Emma just said, "Gleba

336
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:38,340
It's not a word.

337
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:38,340
Ugh. Okay, fine. I'm gonna look it up.

338
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:40,060
Oh, okay, great.

339
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:43,980
While you're at it, she said another word the other day. Why don't you look up:

340
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:54,240
All right. Okay. Okay. Gleba Gleba. Gleba. Gleba!

341
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:59,820
Here it is! "The fleshy, spore-bearing inner mass of a certain fungi."

342
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:04,580
Heh.

343
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:08,170
She's gonna be a scientist.

344
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:17,970
Damn it. Anybody got anything?

345
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:17,970
No.

346
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,300
I'm still looking through mine.

347
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:23,680
Just double-checking. No.

348
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:26,770
No. No.

349
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,650
No!

350
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:39,660
Hello? Hold on.

351
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:40,870
It's your boss.

352
00:18:41,030 --> 00:18:43,830
Ah, the "I'm sorry I rejected you" phone call.

353
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:46,620
I'm not used to getting these from guys.

354
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:50,170
Hey, Steve.

355
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:50,170
Chandler, hi.

356
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:53,250
I'm sure you've heard we filled the three positions.

357
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:55,760
We felt that with your maturity and experience...

358
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:58,380
you wouldn't be happy being someone's assistant.

359
00:18:58,590 --> 00:19:01,180
I'd love to be somebody's assistant. Answering phones...

360
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:03,180
getting coffee, I live for that stuff.

361
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:08,270
And I'm not too mature. Farts, boobies, butt cracks!

362
00:19:10,310 --> 00:19:13,610
Chandler, you were the strongest person in the program.

363
00:19:13,770 --> 00:19:17,240
We're offering you the position of junior copywriter.

364
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,700
Me? That guy who just said, "butt cracks"?

365
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:23,070
Yes, that's right.

366
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:25,620
We're excited about the level of sophistication...

367
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:28,120
you'll be bringing to the job.

368
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:33,210
Okay. Well, thanks, you won't regret it. I'll see you tomorrow.

369
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,350
What?

370
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,480
Oh, yeah, I'm gonna be a junior copywriter!

371
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:54,520
Congratulations! Oh, sweetie, I'm so proud of you.

372
00:19:54,690 --> 00:19:57,320
Thanks. Does that mean I get the good loving tonight?

373
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:01,320
You bet. No TV or anything.

374
00:20:01,990 --> 00:20:05,330
Hey, that is so great about the job.

375
00:20:01,990 --> 00:20:05,330
Thanks, man.

376
00:20:05,490 --> 00:20:07,660
I'd like to think I had something to do with it.

377
00:20:07,870 --> 00:20:11,080
Really? Why?

378
00:20:07,870 --> 00:20:11,080
Well, before with the wishbone.

379
00:20:11,250 --> 00:20:17,000
I, uh, didn't wish we would win the lottery. I wished you'd get the job.

380
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:19,510
Qh, yeah?

381
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:21,880
Don't tell Monica. She'll rip your heart out.

382
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:23,260
Oh, yeah.

383
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:28,510
Well, you know what? There was a little part of me...

384
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,770
that really thought we were gonna win.

385
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:37,440
Me too. So much for my dinosaur Amelia Earhart theme park.

386
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:42,030
You guys? What was the Powerball number again?

387
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,780
Seven.

388
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,780
We won.

389
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:46,870
What?

390
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:46,870
We won!

391
00:20:47,030 --> 00:20:49,740
Let me see! Let me see!

392
00:20:47,030 --> 00:20:49,740
Don't tear it!

393
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:53,920
Phoebe, you don't have any of the first five numbers!

394
00:20:55,000 --> 00:21:01,260
I know that, but look, we got the Powerball number. We won $3!

395
00:21:02,130 --> 00:21:06,220
Wow, you think we should get that over 20 years or go for the big payout?

396
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:11,020
I don't care. I've never won anything before. I can't believe this!

397
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:13,480
So, Pheebs, what are you gonna do with your $3?

398
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:16,810
Well, it's not all mine. We all get 50 cents.

399
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:20,600
Aw. You know what? You can have mine.

400
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:21,900
Me too.

401
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:21,900
Me too.

402
00:21:22,070 --> 00:21:24,400
Me too. Ha, ha.

403
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:32,000
Well, I guess if everybody else is.

404
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:44,420
Hey, guys. So I just called the Powerball hot line.

405
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:49,890
Can you believe it? Nobody won.

406
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:49,890
Um, I beg to differ.

407
00:21:51,390 --> 00:21:55,020
Maybe nobody won the jackpot, but there was this guy in here earlier...

408
00:21:55,180 --> 00:22:00,110
and he found a ticket on the street right outside and won $10,000.

409
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:14,740
Coo. Again, don't blame the pretty lady.

410
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:20,080
It was not her fault. It was me, the pigeon. Coo.

411
00:22:23,630 --> 00:22:26,920
Seriously, stop staring at her.

